    description: "Original motivation of the WI-kuvam audit (orthogonal to the SHAPE_MISMATCH defect itself): there is no single place to see which concept strings YAMLs emit and which linkers consume them. The audit surfaced ~30 INERT_EMIT concepts (YAMLs emit them but no linker consumes — e.g. fastapi's 'dependency'/'background_task'/'request'/'auth'/'security'/'error_handler'/'lifecycle'; django's 'controller'/'serializer'/'form'/'admin'/'event_handler'/'auth_backend'/'permission'/'filter'/'template_tag'/'template_filter'; express's 'auth_strategy'/'websocket_handler'/'websocket_emitter'/'websocket_namespace'/'http_client'; cli's 'option'/'argument'/'entrypoint'/'error'/'output'; celery's 'scheduled_task'/'event_handler'/'configuration').\n\nDeliverable: a concept vocabulary registry that enumerates, per concept string:\n  - Which YAML(s) emit it\n  - Which linker(s) / other consumers read it\n  - Expected shape of the dict emitted (which extra keys populate — 'path', 'method', etc.)\n  - Status: live (≥1 consumer) vs inert (0 consumers, candidate for removal or future linker)\n\nLocation options: docs/CONCEPTS.md (new file), or a section in existing docs/LINKERS.md. Either way, generation should ideally be scripted (grep over YAMLs and linker sources) so the registry stays fresh as new concepts are added.\n\nDeferred from WI-kuvam audit. Blocked by nothing; safe to do in parallel with WI-vogoh/WI-hopij."  # f93a
    fields: {}  # f93a
